# Cursor Rules — Edward Wibowo Portfolio (Next.js 14+ / Tailwind CSS)

## Core Stack & Context Guidelines
- Tech Stack: Next.js 14+ (App Router), JavaScript/React, Tailwind CSS, Lucide React (icons), Framer Motion (animations).
- Animation & Particle Library: Use **[tsparticles-slim]** for background particle effects (performance optimized) and Framer Motion for entrance/hover interactions.
- Strict Rule: Always consult `PORTFOLIO_CONTEXT2.md` prior to generating or modifying any UI components, page structures, or styling logic.

## Design System & Aesthetic Rules
- **Subtle Ambient Space Theme**:
  - Sparse, non-distracting field of small 'stars' (particles) rendered via `tsparticles-slim`.
  - Deep ambient background gradient shifting between deep void (`#05070C`) and muted cosmic purple (`#120A1C`). Must remain monolithic, dark, and executive-ready.
- **Glassmorphic & Structural Framing**:
  - Structural 1.5px glassmorphic borders (`border border-white/10` or `border-neutral-800`) across cards and floating elements.
  - Monospaced labels for technical status indicators (e.g., `SYS.LOC // JAKARTA, ID` | `STATUS // ONLINE`).
- **Hero-Only Warp-Jump Load Animation**:
  - Custom horizontal gradient lines (`from-transparent via-indigo-500 to-transparent`) in the Hero section only.
  - Animates laterally on initial page load (0.6s–0.8s `ease-out`) as an entry effect. All standard section dividers remain clean, static 1px borders (`border-white/10`).
- **Dynamic Accent Theming**:
  - Bind CSS custom properties (`--accent-color`, `--glow-color`) based on runtime data in `projects.json`.
  - On hover, card borders dynamically transition to the active project's accent color with a soft ambient shadow (`shadow-[var(--glow-color)]`).
- **Interactive States**:
  - All clickable or hoverable elements include subtle lift animations (`hover:-translate-y-1`) and smooth transitions (`transition-all duration-300`).

## Component Architecture Standards
Keep components modular, single-responsibility, and easy to maintain:
- `components/StarryBackground.jsx` -> Client component that initializes and renders the optimized `tsparticles-slim` background.
- `components/SiteNavigation.jsx` -> Fixed floating glass pill navbar (`top-6 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2`) with quick-scroll anchors and resume CTA.
- `components/Hero.jsx` -> Hero section featuring academic badge, syntax-highlighted JSON identity block, headline hook, profile headshot glow ring, primary action buttons, and the one-time warp-jump load animation.
- `components/ProjectCard.jsx` -> Case study card implementing the 3-column Purpose & Impact breakdown (Challenge, Approach, Impact) and bottom tech pill matrix.
- `components/ProjectGrid.jsx` -> Direct-impact case study showcase with hover state management.
- `components/ExperienceMatrix.jsx` -> Asymmetric Bento-style layout (BNCC C Praetorian feature card + Samsung Innovation Campus and ElevAIte Hackathon cards).
- `data/projects.json` -> Source-of-truth runtime data feed for project titles, metrics, themes, and links.
- `app/layout.js` -> Main layout structure integrating `StarryBackground` and `SiteNavigation`.

## Coding Best Practices
- Add `'use client'` at the top of components handling active hover states, dynamic CSS variable updates, interactivity, Framer Motion animations, or background particle rendering.
- Ensure all external links include `target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"`.